## Requirements and configuration

- Terraform CLI. Check the [Terraform Registry](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/terr4m/shell/latest) for current compatibility information.
- The machine running Terraform must have the configured interpreter installed. The default is `/bin/bash -c` on non-Windows systems and `pwsh -c` on Windows. Scripts can also require other tools, credentials, filesystem access, and network access.

This provider executes arbitrary configured commands. Use only trusted scripts and configurations. Commands may run during planning, apply, refresh, and destroy. Inputs and outputs may be persisted in Terraform state; avoid passing secrets through them or logging secrets.

Declare the provider in `required_providers` and choose a version constraint for your upgrade policy. For example, `~> 1.0` permits compatible 1.x releases while excluding 2.x:

```terraform
terraform {
  required_providers {
    shell = {
      source  = "terr4m/shell"
      version = "~> 1.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "shell" {}
```

Run `terraform init` to install the provider. See the [Terraform Registry](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/terr4m/shell/latest) for available versions and installation details.

